An extensible Model Context Protocol server for Isabelle
=======================================================

isabelle mcp_server serves JSON-RPC over stdin/stdout and keeps one prover session
for theory checking and user-declared ML tools. Progress goes to stderr.

Requirements and installation
-----------------------------
Use Isabelle2025-2 and register this repository's mcp component:

    isabelle components -u /absolute/path/to/isabelle-mcp/mcp
    isabelle build -b MCP-HOL
    isabelle mcp_server -s MCP-HOL -T MCP

Supply -T THEORY to select the theory whose tools the server exposes. The server
always creates a private temporary wrapper theory importing exactly that selected
theory through PIDE, whether the selected theory is in the image or in source.
The wrapper's context supplies the catalogue and default execution context.
Bootstrap waits for its successful final end and validates the bridge before
Ready. Its document requirement persists until shutdown; bridge work drains
before release and session stop. Reprocessing ancestors and then the wrapper
updates later catalogues. There is no source/image split or heap-root fallback.
The bridge identifies the current wrapper evaluation on every hello/call; invalid
or stale selections fail without falling back to an earlier catalogue.

Startup diagnostics
-------------------
Run with -v to include Isabelle-resolved heap inputs on stderr:

    isabelle mcp_server -v -s MCP-HOL -T MCP-HOL.MCP

"reused" means Isabelle's no-build check accepted the saved session image and
its dependencies. "build required" means that check did not succeed; the normal
Isabelle build then runs. "build completed" reports successful completion of
that build operation, not whether an image was missing versus outdated.

Verbose output reports the installation, session source directory, selected
theory and ordered heap input paths through Isabelle's APIs. The paths use the
same resource Store and session background as headless startup; they report
resolved inputs, not an observation of operating-system file opens. MCP-HOL
includes the MCP-Tools theories but does not load a separate MCP-Tools parent
heap. No build UUID or invalidation reason is guessed or read from a database.

A reused image still requires prover startup and processing of the temporary
bridge-root theory. This is not a rebuild of the saved MCP session. Unexpected
heap paths should be investigated using the same Isabelle launcher and user
settings as the server. stdout remains exclusively the JSON-RPC channel.

Library discovery is initialized on demand. The first tool needing full-library
session/theory information performs dependency analysis; later calls reuse it.
The documentation catalogue initializes independently on its first use. Reading
a manual may also require dependency analysis. Concurrent callers share each
successful initialization; a failed initialization can be retried by a later call.
The selected session's own build checks and PIDE preparation still run at startup.

Tools
-----
- load_theory loads/re-checks disk theories with dependencies and reports
  positioned errors and warnings through headless session.use_theories; it
  re-reads the file fresh on every call, so calling it again after an edit
  is already a "check" -- there is no separate check_theory.
- unload_theory removes a loaded theory; image theories cannot be unloaded.
- list_sessions and list_theories discover the session library.
- search_sources searches theory names by substring, not source contents.
- doc_list and doc_read discover and read documentation.

The server also advertises active ML tools declared with mcp_tool in the root's
import chain. Keep ordinary Isabelle mcp_tools activation and bundles in theory
text. Tool declaration changes emit notifications/tools/list_changed. The root
selects the implementation; an ML-resolved invocation target supplies its
Proof.context. Every ML tool automatically advertises an optional string argument
named context. Supply its target URL in the ordinary arguments object; omit it
to execute at the root. The framework resolves the URL and removes context before
calling the unchanged ML implementation. Tool declarations cannot define their
own context parameter. The seven Scala builtins do not receive this parameter.

Testing
-------
Register mcp_test as another component to use isabelle mcp_test. Test layers are
scala-unit, heap and bridge; -L all selects all three. ML theory tests and the
Python e2e runner cover the other retained layers. Consult
.agents/skills/isabelle-execution/SKILL.md for installation selection and private
worktree state. The repository acceptance command is:

    tools/planning-gate done

Static metadata or a focused test run does not establish full acceptance.
See SERVER_CARVE_OUT_PLAN.md for the approved cut and plans/ for surviving
contracts. Replacement proof tooling and configurable availability are deferred.

Current boundary: reply-size, admission and lifecycle protections are retained.
A request-byte guard was absent in the baseline and remains explicitly deferred;
the carve-out does not claim that protection.
